A small coil is placed close to one end of a solenoid connected to a power supply. The plane of the small coil is normal to the axis of the solenoid, as illustrated in Fig. 9.1.
{{figure:figure_9_1.png}}
The power supply causes the current $I$ in the solenoid to vary with time $t$ as shown in Fig. 9.2.
{{figure:figure_9_2.png}}
